    "curated_prompt": "Explicit TinyDB.close inside a context closes the storage twice\n\nCalling `close()` explicitly inside a TinyDB context should close the storage once. Exiting that context should complete successfully.\n\n```python\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB\n\nclass TestStorage:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.closed = False\n\n    def read(self):\n        return {}\n\n    def write(self, data):\n        pass\n\n    def close(self):\n        if self.closed:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Storage already closed!\")\n        self.closed = True\n\nwith TinyDB(storage=TestStorage) as db:\n    db.close()\n```\n\nThe `storage` argument above is the storage class accepted by TinyDB. The current code raises `RuntimeError(\"Storage already closed!\")` on context exit. The explicit close and context cleanup should work together without closing this storage twice.\n",
